{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.send()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State(observer:)"},{"type":"text","text":" packs, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State.apply(_:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" unpacks."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accessor checks ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_modify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accessor (used by ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cross-slice observation isolation."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro generates a separate ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" class for each ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property. A view reading ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.items","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" won’t re-render when only ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.ui","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates the observer class tree and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" warns if ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means ","type":"text"},{"code":"send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Reducer-Weight","text":"Reducer Weight","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Effect-Threading","level":2,"text":"Effect Threading","type":"heading"},{"style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"code":"Process.waitUntilExit()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Thread.sleep()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"Architecture & Performance","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"anchor":"Explanation","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxObservable":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SwiduxObservable","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Bridges a value-type state struct to an "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" class tree for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-property SwiftUI observation granularity."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxobservable","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"PersistencePlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, payw